{:created 1787709700711, :description "Foreign-format readers for vaelii — OpenCyc, RDF/OWL, WordNet, OBO and\n                ATOMIC, each translated into one corpus format, discovered through\n                vaelii's plugin seam.", :group_name "com.vaelii", :jar_name "vaelii-foreign", :version "0.13.0"}
{:created 1787709800281, :description "Postgres targets for vaelii's storage seams, in two independent\n                lanes. The record store (vaelii.postgres.record-store) puts a KB's\n                durable ground truth in a database — core selects it as :pg-memory\n                or :pg-disk-log — with COPY on the bulk path, a fetch LRU in front of a\n                round-trip point read, and cursor-streamed enumerations. The\n                snapshot sink (vaelii.postgres.snapshot) is a SnapshotSink /\n                SnapshotSource, so a KB image — the index projection today, any of\n                io.snapshot's named sections — lands in a database as a few bulk\n                transactions and reads back the same way. An Apache-2.0 adapter on\n                the SSPL engine, depending on core, never depended on by it.", :group_name "com.vaelii", :jar_name "postgres", :version "0.13.0"}
{:created 1787709841830, :description "SQLite targets for vaelii's storage seams. The first is the\n                snapshot sink (vaelii.sqlite.snapshot): a SnapshotSink /\n                SnapshotSource over a single SQLite file, so a KB image — the index\n                projection today, any of io.snapshot's named sections — lands in a\n                zero-configuration file as a few bulk transactions and reads back\n                the same way. An Apache-2.0 adapter on the SSPL engine, depending on\n                core, never depended on by it.", :group_name "com.vaelii", :jar_name "sqlite", :version "0.13.0"}
